  "notes": "{味方|みかた} refers to someone on your side — an ally, supporter, or friend. As a noun it describes the person or group that supports you; as a suru verb it means to take someone's side.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {味方|みかた}になる: to become an ally\n- {味方|みかた}につく: to take someone's side\n- {味方|みかた}する: to side with someone\n- {敵|てき}か{味方|みかた}か: friend or foe\n- {強|つよ}い{味方|みかた}: a strong ally/supporter\n\nUSAGE:\nThe verb form {味方|みかた}する takes the person being supported with を: {弟|おとうと}を{味方|みかた}する (to side with one's younger brother).\n\nHOMOPHONE:\nDistinguish from {見方|みかた} (point of view, way of looking at things) — same reading, different kanji and meaning.",
